page('credits.html','Image Credits & Prototype Notes | DMS Studio','Image sources and editorial notes for the DMS Studio website prototype.',intro('Credits & notes','Made with <em>care.</em>')+'<div class="article-body"><h2>Project photography</h2><p>Babbar Residency, Opera Home and Essentia Salon photographs are from the existing DMS Studio portfolio. Yogesh Residence photographs are based on images supplied for this website update; selected views received careful colour and detail enhancement, and the uploaded source files remain unchanged. The Essentia Salon banner is a restrained photographic colour and crop adjustment of the supplied storefront image; its original is retained. Photography credit: DMS Studio.</p><h2>Prototype content</h2><p>The DMS Studio journal provides practical planning guides. Project references are linked to their case studies, while general guidance is not a project specification. The interactive house is an original architectural concept with CC0 material textures from Poly Haven, not a scan of a completed DMS project. The earlier stylised house is retained in the backup archive. The logo uses the centre of the supplied DMS artwork without its circular border. No review ratings, awards or guarantees have been invented.</p><h2>Reference assets</h2><p>Two optional reference images are included in the editable asset library: Taylor Heery and Parth Savani via Unsplash. They are not presented as DMS projects. Homepage, service and journal imagery now use separately credited Unsplash photographs as editorial inspiration. These are not DMS commissions. Full photo links and credits are in assets/editorial-sources.json.</p><h2>Privacy</h2><p>This static prototype does not store enquiries or use analytics cookies. Enquiry details are processed by FormSubmit to deliver them to DMS Studio by email. External links are subject to the destination’s own policies.</p></div>',active='')
